# `project-rename` of an unknown column is DS1001; a new name that another column has is DS1005.
mode: check
show: schema
schema: 'orders.csv'(orderId: string, customerId: string, amount: real, qty: long, timestamp: datetime)
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | project-rename total = amout;
from 'orders.csv' | project-rename amount = qty
---- expected
error[DS1001]: unknown column `amout`
  --> query:1:44
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | project-rename total = amout;
  |                                            ^^^^^ no column named `amout` here
  |
  = help: a column with a similar name exists: `amount`
  = note: columns available at this point: orderId, customerId, amount, qty, timestamp

error[DS1005]: duplicate column name `amount`
  --> query:2:36
  |
2 | from 'orders.csv' | project-rename amount = qty
  |                                    ^^^^^^ there is already a column `amount`
  |
  = help: pick a name no other column has, or remove `amount` first with `project-away amount`

query 1 columns:
  orderId: string
  customerId: string
  amount: real
  qty: long
  timestamp: datetime

query 2 columns:
  orderId: string
  customerId: string
  amount: real
  qty: long
  timestamp: datetime
